---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/url";
---

<Layout
  title="Methodology"
  active="methodology"
  description="How the NZ Tech-for-Good directory is built, verified, and maintained."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Methodology</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      How this directory is built, verified, and maintained — for
      researchers, journalists, and anyone who wants to understand
      what is behind the data.
    </p>

    <h2>How entries are chosen</h2>
    <p>
      See <a href={url("/docs/how-entries-are-chosen/")}>How entries are chosen</a> for
      the full scope criteria. In short: NZ-based, technology is central to what
      they do, and the primary mission is public benefit.
    </p>

    <h2>How entries are verified</h2>
    <p>
      Every field in every entry is checked against a live, public source before
      it is added. If a fact cannot be confirmed, the field is left empty rather
      than guessed. The <code>source</code> field on each entry records exactly
      what was checked and how.
    </p>
    <p>
      Links are checked automatically every week via
      <a href="https://github.com/olitreadwell/nz-tech-for-good/blob/main/scripts/linkcheck.py">scripts/linkcheck.py</a>,
      which opens a tracking issue on genuine dead links and closes it when they
      recover.
    </p>

    <h2>How the data is structured</h2>
    <p>
      The directory is built from open data files: one YAML file per organisation
      in <code>data/entries/</code>, shaped by a JSON Schema at
      <code>schema/entry.schema.json</code>. Every entry must pass schema
      validation (<code>python3 scripts/validate.py</code>) before it can be
      merged.
    </p>

    <h2>Machine-readable data</h2>
    <p>
      The full directory is exported as
      <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/olitreadwell/nz-tech-for-good/main/data/exports/entries.json">JSON</a>
      and
      <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/olitreadwell/nz-tech-for-good/main/data/exports/entries.csv">CSV</a>,
      regenerated by CI on every push. An
      <a href={url("/api.json")}>API endpoint</a> serves the JSON directly
      from the site.
    </p>

    <h2>How to cite</h2>
    <p>
      APA: <em>NZ Tech-for-Good</em>. (2026). Retrieved [date] from
      https://olitreadwell.github.io/nz-tech-for-good/
    </p>
    <p>
      MLA: "NZ Tech-for-Good." 2026, olitreadwell.github.io/nz-tech-for-good/.
    </p>
    <p>
      Individual entries can be cited using the 📝 Cite button on each entry
      page.
    </p>

    <h2>Licence</h2>
    <p>
      Code is <a href="https://github.com/olitreadwell/nz-tech-for-good/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT</a>.
      Data is
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>:
      reuse and share it, including commercially, as long as you credit this
      project and share alike.
    </p>

    <h2>Contributing</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/olitreadwell/nz-tech-for-good/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Read the contributor guide</a>
      for how to suggest or add an entry, or browse
      <a href="https://github.com/olitreadwell/nz-tech-for-good/issues?q=is%3Aissue+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22">good first issues</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
